<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bairén</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1097">1097</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bairén was fought in January 1097 near Gandia, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a>, supported by King Peter I of Aragon, and an Almoravid army. The Christians defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>, securing El Cid's hold on Valencia and the coastal route to the south.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bairen.jpg" alt="Battle of Bairén" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cid.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
